codex
The fresh mutation compiled (`--dry-run` exit 0) and then failed for the intended reason (`WarnStuckClaimState`, exit 1, with the executed result `true` unable to satisfy the mutated target `false`). So the proof is result-sensitive, but non-vacuity does not cure the false proof rule. I’m consolidating the rule-by-rule inventory, trust ledger, and final seven-stage review now.
